# TrackLLM

> TrackLLM continuously monitors LLM APIs for undisclosed changes, using logprob
> tracking (LT) where logprobs are exposed and black-box border input tracking
> (B3IT) where they aren't. Every HTML page on this site has a markdown twin at
> the same path (X.html → X.md) with the same content and absolute links — read
> those instead of the HTML.

Endpoint slugs are stable: `<model>#<provider>` with every character outside `{{ SLUG_KEPT_CHARS }}` replaced by its two-digit hex code — `/` → `2f`, `#` → `23`, `:` → `3a` (so `moonshotai/kimi-k3:free` at `chutes/fp8` is `moonshotai2fkimi-k33afree23chutes2ffp8`); an endpoint's page is `endpoints/<slug>.md`.

## Start here

- [Homepage]({{ SITE_URL }}/index.md): live stats, the latest changes, the most drift-prone providers and most-changed endpoints
- [Change log]({{ SITE_URL }}/changes.md): every detected change with magnitude and description
- [Providers]({{ SITE_URL }}/providers.md): every provider company with its LT drift rate and monitoring volume
- [All endpoints]({{ SITE_URL }}/endpoints.md): every endpoint in the catalog with its tracking status and change count
- [Methodology]({{ SITE_URL }}/methodology.md): how LT and B3IT work, the detection rules and thresholds, links to both papers
- [Sitemap]({{ SITE_URL }}/sitemap.xml): every HTML page

## Data

- [overview.json]({{ SITE_URL }}/data/overview.json): stats, endpoint directory, provider rates
- [changes.json]({{ SITE_URL }}/data/changes.json): every detected change, newest first
- [changes_page.json]({{ SITE_URL }}/data/changes_page.json): change log with descriptions
- per-model `data/models/<slug>.json` (full drift/TV series per endpoint), per-provider `data/providers/<slug>.json`, per-endpoint `data/b3it/<slug>/b3it.json`
- [Raw data repository]({{ DATA_REPO_URL }}): every collected API response, committed hourly
- [Code repository]({{ CODE_REPO_URL }}): the collector and the generator that builds this site

